              "text": "**\"Still in Love with You\"** is a track by the legendary country music duo **Brooks & Dunn**, featured on their landmark debut studio album, ***Brand New Man***, released on August 13, 1991. \n\nHere is everything you need to know about the song, including its lyrics, background, and some interesting trivia:\n\n### 1. The Lyrics\nThe song tells a melancholic story of departure and lingering love, with the narrator preparing to leave for Baton Rouge but realizing they can never truly move on from their partner.\n\n> **[Verse 1]**\n> *My taxicab is waiting*\n> *Wish I could hold you one last time*\n> *After all we've had together*\n> *There's gotta be a better way of telling you goodbye*\n> \n> **[Chorus]**\n> *If I had a horse, I'd ride off in the sunset*\n> *If I had wings, I'd fly off in the sky so blue*\n> *If I had the time, I'd spend my whole life dreaming*\n> *But I'd wake up, still in love with you*\n> \n> **[Verse 2]**\n> *Be in Baton Rouge by morning*\n> *Hope you're missing me by then*\n> *I'd like to be the kind of memory*\n> *That makes you want to take me back in your arms again*\n> \n> **[Bridge]**\n> *Some nights when you get lonely*\n> *Will you still remember me?*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Key Facts & Trivia\n* **Kix Brooks on Lead Vocals:** While Ronnie Dunn sang lead vocals on the vast majority of Brooks & Dunn's biggest radio hits, their early albums featured a more even split. \"Still in Love with You\" is one of the gems from their debut album where **Kix Brooks** takes the lead vocals. \n* **The Writers:** The track was co-written by Kix Brooks, Ronnie Dunn, and their frequent collaborator and producer, Don Cook.\n* **B-Side Track:** Though \"Still in Love with You\" was never promoted as an A-side radio single itself, it served as the B-side to their second consecutive #1 hit single, \"My Next Broken Heart,\" released in September 1991.\n\n---\n\n### *Note on a Similar Song:*\nIf you are looking for Ronnie Dunn's solo work, he released a cover of the classic Hank Williams song **\"I Can't Help It (If I'm Still in Love with You)\"** on his 2020 solo album, *Re-Dunn*. However, the original Brooks & Dunn track from 1991 is a completely different, original song!",
